## Operational Quality

| Area | Rule |
| --- | --- |
| Local Git baseline | `fetch.prune=true`, `pull.ff=only`, `remote.pushDefault=backup`, `push.default=current`, and `push.autoSetupRemote=true`; local `main` tracks `backup/main`, while `origin` remains a fallback remote. |
| GitHub repository policy | `main` requires a PR, permits merge commits only, blocks force pushes and deletion, keeps automatic head-branch deletion enabled, and allows PR branch updates. |
| Post-merge cleanup | After a user merges a PR, the next task verifies the PR state, fetches `backup --prune`, synchronizes local `main` with `backup/main`, and deletes only the matching merged local branch for the PR just handled. Older unrelated branches are never deleted automatically. |
| Release branch audit | The release check reports local and `backup/*` remote-tracking branches already contained in `backup/main`; additional cleanup requires an explicit scope. |
| Layout System v2 | Meaningful layout contracts are documented in `Docs/Master_Spec`, listed in `Docs/Generic_Component_Catalog`, implemented in `TypeScript/CSS/rules-grid.ts` and `TypeScript/CSS/rules-layout.ts`, and generated to `UI/grid.css` and `UI/layout.css`. |
| Interaction readiness | Dialog, drawer, popover, toast, progress, skeleton, data state, bulk feedback, stepper, and filter builder classes remain catalog-listed and check-covered. |
| Advanced Input and Design-System UI | Keyboard tabs, combobox, multi-select, segmented control, radio card group, switch group, range input, token add/remove, dirty/touched validation, date picker, tree view, data grid, pagination, saved views, column visibility, selection counters, property inspector, token swatch, component preview, and bottom sheet classes are catalog-listed, generated from TypeScript source, sample-covered, and check-covered. |
